  "body": "**What fails:** `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp_live -- idle_timeout::a_configured_finite_window_expires_on_the_listener` fails on Windows. It failed on two separate Windows check boxes (winnie, at main `1c0152c9`, and bacon, at `b0936fb8`), after about 6 s each time. The Linux post-merge gate passes it.\n\n**Where it came from:** the test was added by PR #4190 (fix(mcp): configure the live client idle timeout), merged 2026-11-26.\n\n**Likely cause (not confirmed):** the finite idle window expiring on the listener depends on socket/listener timing that behaves differently on Windows (named pipe or loopback accept timing). The local Windows check logs keep only the summary line, so the panic text is not captured; a run on a Windows box gives it.\n\nDone means: the test passes on Windows (or is made OS-independent), with the reason recorded.\n",
